  "_about": "a giant anteater SCULPTED on its rig (2026-11-05, gen: scratchpad sc/new6/anteater.py): a deep, narrow body 0.6 m at the shoulder; the head drawn out into a long, tubular, slightly down-curved snout -- head and snout a third of the head-and-body -- with tiny eyes and small round ears; coarse grizzled grey-brown hair, the hind legs dark; the bold black band from the throat diagonally back and up over the shoulder to a point on the back, edged in white on both sides (painted per pixel: the `anteater` pattern); pale forelegs with a black band at the wrist, knuckle-walking on the outer edge of the fists, the great fore claws curled in under them; and a huge bushy flag of a tail, long hair hanging in a tall flat sheet SHARP PASS 2 (2026-11-08): the pointed parts -- claw, nail (6 in all) -- are the engine's sharp `horn`s (sharp.js), made from the field shapes they replaced by tools/creaturegen/sharp/ (claws.py, teeth.py, spikes.py, antlers.py, bills.py): rooted in the body, tips pointed; RE-RUN those after this species' generator. (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur. (2026-11-08, ears2.py) The EARS (ears2.py): small round cupped sheets (sharp.js `fin`); the roots faired. (2026-11-08, review.py: fore claws) The FORE CLAWS (review.py anteater_claws): the 2nd and 3rd digits' long curved digging claws, ~11 cm and three quarters of that, arching out of the top of the fist's front, down round it close to it and curling back under it toward the ground (folded, as it walks on its knuckles); deep and narrow (aspect 2), dark at the base.",
